spec:
One PR on the replay stage layout and canvas input. It changes behaviour for every ReplayStage and MapReplayer host: the game page, ReviewReplayPanel (mobileCompact), CompactReplayHost and the public pages. Fullscreen behaviour is unchanged.

Roadmap interplay: game-nav-and-replay-controls (W3) later adds shortcuts and persisted prefs to ReplayStage and TransportDock. It must persist the new panel state from here. accurate-playback-smooth (W3) owns the SegmentedReplayHost overlays and the in-canvas accuracy note, so leave those alone. replayer-studio (W6) adds tap-to-inspect and must keep the wheel gating defined here. Uses --chrome-bottom from app-shell-quick-fixes (W1) when present.

1) Mobile layout (apps/web/components/analyzer/game/replay/ReplayStage.tsx)
- Below xl, the order becomes: top bar → map band → TransportDock → one 'Production | Build order' panel. Today the dock is rendered after both rails (ReplayStage.tsx:313-337), up to about 36rem below the map.
- Render the dock once and place it with grid-template-areas or order classes inside the same container. Breakpoint-specific areas: below xl, map / dock / panel; at xl, the current three columns with the dock underneath.
- On phones, make the dock `sticky bottom-[var(--chrome-bottom,0px)]` with pb-[env(safe-area-inset-bottom)], so it never sits under the mobile tab bar. The stage root uses overflow-hidden, which breaks sticky; switch it to overflow-clip (it clips rounded corners without creating a scroll container).
- Replace the two stacked rails below xl (ReplayStage.tsx:261, 308; both expanded by default at :159-160) with one segmented panel:
  - role=tablist with 'Production' and 'Build order' tabs, the same roving-tabindex keyboard pattern as the ProductionRail fix, and only one rail rendered at a time;
  - collapsed by default below md: a 44px disclosure row 'Show production & build order' with a chevron, aria-expanded;
  - expanded by default from md to xl.
- At xl, both side rails stay as today and the ReplaySettings rail toggles keep working. mobileCompact keeps hiding the rails entirely.
- Readability: raise the ReplayTopBar stat captions (10px) and the TransportDock phase-band labels (text-[0.5625rem], TransportDock.tsx:164) to the text-micro token (12px). When a phase band is too narrow, hide its label rather than shrinking it.

2) Scroll and touch (apps/web/components/analyzer/game/MapReplayer.tsx)
- Outside fullscreen (fullscreenRef.current false), onWheel (MapReplayer.tsx:785-788) zooms only if one of these is true:
  - e.ctrlKey || e.metaKey (trackpad pinch arrives as a ctrlKey wheel in Chromium and Firefox; also handle Safari gesturestart/gesturechange);
  - the canvas has focus: give it tabIndex=0; a click focuses it, and blur, Escape or pointer-leave releases it.
- Otherwise do not call preventDefault, so the page scrolls, and show a 1.5 s overlay hint 'Hold Ctrl to zoom' ('Hold ⌘ to zoom' on Mac). The hint is throttled and aria-hidden; the canvas aria-describedby text mentions the control.
- In fullscreen, keep the current always-zoom behaviour.
- Touch: replace the static touch-none class (MapReplayer.tsx:1003) with a touch-action style set from the view state: 'pan-y' while view.z <= 1 (a one-finger swipe scrolls the page; pinch still reaches the pointer handlers and zooms), and 'none' while zoomed (a one-finger drag pans, as at MapReplayer.tsx:820). Update it in applyZoom and resetView. Double-click and double-tap reset are unchanged.

Tests:
- replay/__tests__/ReplayStageLayout.test.tsx:
  - below xl, the DOM order is map band, dock, panel;
  - only one rail renders;
  - the panel is collapsed when matchMedia('(max-width: 767px)') matches;
  - at xl both rails render;
  - mobileCompact hides the panel.
- ReplayFullscreen.test.tsx / MapReplayerControlled.test.tsx:
  - a plain wheel event is not defaultPrevented, the zoom is unchanged and the hint is shown;
  - Ctrl+wheel zooms;
  - a wheel on a focused canvas zooms;
  - a plain wheel in fullscreen zooms;
  - canvas.style.touchAction is 'pan-y' at z=1 and 'none' after zooming.

